Go module dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Direct and transitive dependencies are declared in go.mod and fetched by the Go
toolchain. Every one is permissively licensed (MIT, BSD-3-Clause, or Apache-2.0);
none is copyleft. Their full license texts travel with the modules themselves in
the module cache. Notable direct dependencies:

  github.com/alecthomas/kong                       MIT
  github.com/sabhiram/go-gitignore                 MIT
  github.com/sugarme/tokenizer                     Apache-2.0
  github.com/yalue/onnxruntime_go                  MIT
  github.com/yuin/goldmark                         MIT
  go.yaml.in/yaml/v3                               MIT and Apache-2.0
  modernc.org/sqlite                               BSD-3-Clause

  github.com/rogpeppe/go-internal                  BSD-3-Clause
      Used by the end-to-end script tests only; not linked into the binary.
      https://github.com/rogpeppe/go-internal

The tree-sitter runtime and every grammar are C compiled into the binary, so
their attribution ships with each release rather than being fetched at run time:

